     "i": "ti-layout",
     "h": "<div class=\"pblk\">Document, four chapters. (Source: prototype v4 template. Confidence: high for Ch1 and Ch2)</div><div class=\"bul\"><span class=\"dot\">1.</span><span><b>Project context:</b> In short; Project basics (table); Objective and why now; Site description and land use; Planned interventions; Land rights and existing commitments; Provisional service screen (Include, Confirm or Omit, evidence, confidence); Source coverage (what is missing); Constraints and dependencies; Open questions (client, then GY).</span></div><div class=\"bul\"><span class=\"dot\">2.</span><span><b>Demand:</b> overall verdict and source line, then one section per service (Carbon peatland, Carbon woodland, Carbon soil, BNG, Voluntary biodiversity, NFM, Water quality, Replenish), each with a verdict and a table: Buyer, Why relevant, Hook, Relationship status, Source.</span></div><div class=\"bul\"><span class=\"dot\">3.</span><span><b>Supply:</b> one Ecosystem Service Card per included service: rule book, eligibility, volume, price, indicative revenue, funding, confidence, next step. Untested.</span></div><div class=\"bul\"><span class=\"dot\">4.</span><span><b>Summary:</b> caveats first, markets ranked by strength of demand, recommended next step, one page. No pursue or park: the client has committed. Untested.</span></div>"
