     "h": "<div class=\"dtwrap\"><table class=\"dtbl\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"m\">Owner</td><td><span class=\"nmen\"><i class=\"ti ti-user\"></i>Fran Brosnahan</span> (Fran Brosnahan), also the expert. (Source: Thomas, 29 Oct. Confidence: high)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"m\">Expert</td><td><span class=\"nmen\"><i class=\"ti ti-user\"></i>Fran Brosnahan</span> (Fran Brosnahan), drafting the ECT Commercial Strategy and co-built Walkham Valley. Caitlin Ciceri and Harry Forman as secondary experts (Harry and Caitlin built the original Commercial Strategy skill). (Source: Granola 12 Oct, 22 Oct, 29 Oct. Confidence: medium)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"m\">Real examples</td><td>Denton (final, May 2025); Heath to Sea v2; Upper Dee (final); ECT draft v0.1 (15 Oct 2026, 5 estates); Walkham Valley carbon and BNG sales strategies; [WIP] Commercial Strategy Template; Harry's gy-commercial-strategy skill. Links under Sources. (Source: Google Drive search 29 Oct. Confidence: high)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"m\">Why good is hard</td><td>Done differently by different people: Harry's skill (about 9 months old, fixed 10-section structure) and Fran's ECT structure (vision, markets, revenue streams per estate) differ. Too complex and needs distilling: many services, jurisdictions and, for ECT, 5 estates in one document. (Source: Granola 6, 12, 15 Oct; gy-commercial-strategy skill. Confidence: medium)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"m\">Method</td><td>For now: start from Fran's latest skeleton (ECT draft v0.1) as the base Template, and test it against Denton, Heath to Sea and Upper Dee later (side-by-side comparison, then a short workshop with Fran). (Source: Thomas, 29 Oct. Confidence: high)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
